1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,920
Good morning, everyone.

2
00:00:02,370 --> 00:00:03,660
I'm Hyuntae Kim.

3
00:00:04,110 --> 00:00:08,160
Today, I will share JEI's
core repositioning strategy.

4
00:00:08,860 --> 00:00:10,970
Let me start with our key conclusion.

5
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:16,540
JEI must move beyond competing on
workbooks, scale, and digital features.

6
00:00:16,990 --> 00:00:19,868
Our goal is to become the
brand that designs learning

7
00:00:19,922 --> 00:00:22,800
to develop children's ability
to learn independently.

8
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:27,400
I will explain the market changes,
customer needs, the competitive

9
00:00:27,459 --> 00:00:31,240
gap, our positioning, and the
strategic actions we need to take.

10
00:00:32,690 --> 00:00:35,180
First, let’s look at
the challenges we face.

11
00:00:35,630 --> 00:00:37,380
Three changes are important.

12
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:40,750
First, the limitations
of our business scale.

13
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:43,810
JEI ranks fourth in the workbook market.

14
00:00:44,260 --> 00:00:49,100
We have about 300 locations, while
some competitors have more than 700.

15
00:00:49,550 --> 00:00:51,950
It is difficult to compete based on size.

16
00:00:52,650 --> 00:00:54,610
Second, changes in the market.

17
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:59,600
There are fewer children entering school,
but spending per child is increasing.

18
00:01:00,050 --> 00:01:02,702
This means there are fewer
customers, but parents

19
00:01:02,756 --> 00:01:05,570
are willing to spend more
when they see clear value.

20
00:01:06,270 --> 00:01:08,990
Third, similar features
across competitors.

21
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:12,406
AI-based assessment,
personalized learning paths,

22
00:01:12,466 --> 00:01:15,250
and grading have now
become standard features.

23
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:18,354
As these features become
increasingly common,

24
00:01:18,413 --> 00:01:20,890
we need a different basis for competition.

25
00:01:21,340 --> 00:01:25,420
This is why Learning Design is central
to our repositioning strategy.

26
00:01:26,870 --> 00:01:29,530
So, what are parents
really willing to pay for?

27
00:01:29,980 --> 00:01:32,800
We can understand parents’
needs in three layers.

28
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:37,619
The first layer is functional needs:
learning materials for different

29
00:01:37,678 --> 00:01:41,200
levels, connections to school
curricula, and learning data.

30
00:01:41,650 --> 00:01:44,030
The second layer is emotional needs.

31
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:47,700
Parents want to worry less about
their children falling behind.

32
00:01:48,150 --> 00:01:51,110
They also want someone to take
care of their children’s learning.

33
00:01:51,810 --> 00:01:56,280
The third and most important layer is
children’s ability to learn on their own.

34
00:01:56,980 --> 00:01:59,820
Why do parents discontinue
learning programs?

35
00:02:00,270 --> 00:02:03,290
Children may become bored
with repetitive activities.

36
00:02:03,740 --> 00:02:07,700
Standardized learning pace does
not always meet individual needs.

37
00:02:08,150 --> 00:02:10,768
Parents struggle to see
clear learning outcomes

38
00:02:10,824 --> 00:02:13,720
or understand what their
children should learn next.

39
00:02:14,170 --> 00:02:16,948
And much of the responsibility
for managing their

40
00:02:17,005 --> 00:02:19,670
children's learning still
falls on the parents.

41
00:02:20,370 --> 00:02:22,490
These reasons point to one problem.

42
00:02:22,940 --> 00:02:26,060
The problem is not simply a
lack of learning materials.

43
00:02:26,510 --> 00:02:29,985
Parents need a clearer understanding
of what their children should

44
00:02:30,038 --> 00:02:33,460
learn next, why it matters, and
how their learning will progress.

45
00:02:33,910 --> 00:02:36,794
This is why we must shift
our focus from workbooks

46
00:02:36,852 --> 00:02:39,390
to how children’s ability
to learn improves.

47
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:44,630
Now, let’s look at whether our
competitors are meeting this need.

48
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:48,250
These evaluations are based
on customer perceptions.

49
00:02:48,950 --> 00:02:53,120
Each of our three major competitors is
associated with a different strength.

50
00:02:53,570 --> 00:02:58,829
Daekyo emphasizes level-based learning,
Kumon is known for repetition and building

51
00:02:58,893 --> 00:03:03,960
study habits, and Woongjin focuses on
online and AI-powered learning platforms.

52
00:03:04,660 --> 00:03:07,770
Daekyo does not have a clear
long-term learning plan.

53
00:03:08,220 --> 00:03:11,940
Kumon can become boring, causing
children to lose interest.

54
00:03:12,390 --> 00:03:16,103
Woongjin's platform may feel
complex, while screen-based learning

55
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:19,530
can raise concerns about
insufficient handwriting practice.

56
00:03:20,230 --> 00:03:23,785
Above all, no company clearly
answers the question parents

57
00:03:23,846 --> 00:03:27,830
really ask: “Where should my child’s
learning be in three years?”

58
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:30,050
This is where “Design” comes in.

59
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:33,075
It means setting a
direction after diagnosis

60
00:03:33,134 --> 00:03:36,060
and helping children stay
motivated along the way.

61
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:40,524
According to Al Ries’s positioning
principles, it is very difficult

62
00:03:40,580 --> 00:03:44,400
for a company ranked fourth to beat
the leader in the same category.

63
00:03:44,850 --> 00:03:48,502
Rather than trying to move up
the existing competitive ladder,

64
00:03:48,561 --> 00:03:52,449
JEI aims to establish a new ladder
centered on Learning Design—one

65
00:03:52,508 --> 00:03:55,630
where we can build a distinctive
leadership position.

66
00:03:57,080 --> 00:04:00,760
We will move from selling workbooks
to providing Learning Design.

67
00:04:01,210 --> 00:04:04,647
We aim to provide personalized
learning roadmaps that help

68
00:04:04,706 --> 00:04:08,320
each child understand what to
learn next and how to progress.

69
00:04:09,020 --> 00:04:12,876
We will build on our existing
strengths: the JEI Self-Learning

70
00:04:12,938 --> 00:04:16,980
Method, diagnostic assessment, and
structured learning materials.

71
00:04:17,430 --> 00:04:21,940
But we will define self-learning as an
ability, not just the act of studying.

72
00:04:22,390 --> 00:04:26,940
This builds on the nearly 50-year
legacy of the JEI Self-Learning Method.

73
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:32,010
Our focus is not simply to have more
locations or members than competitors.

74
00:04:32,460 --> 00:04:35,878
We want to create clear learning
paths for individual students

75
00:04:35,933 --> 00:04:38,800
and become a leader in the
Learning Design category.

76
00:04:40,250 --> 00:04:43,907
Our proposed positioning statement
is: "JEI designs learning

77
00:04:43,968 --> 00:04:47,260
to develop children's ability
to learn independently."

78
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:51,571
This statement reflects our shift
from simply providing workbooks

79
00:04:51,626 --> 00:04:55,570
to developing children's Self-Learning
Ability through Learning Design.

80
00:04:56,270 --> 00:04:58,850
Our brand messaging is
built around two key

81
00:04:58,910 --> 00:05:01,730
concepts: "Design" and
"Self-Learning Ability."

82
00:05:02,430 --> 00:05:07,108
We have proposed several slogan options,
including "Learning starts with design,"

83
00:05:07,166 --> 00:05:11,670
"Studying starts with design," and "Beyond
Workbooks. Toward Learning Design."

84
00:05:12,370 --> 00:05:14,985
Our proposed campaign
message is: "It's not a

85
00:05:15,043 --> 00:05:17,890
lack of ability. It's a
lack of learning design."

86
00:05:18,590 --> 00:05:21,311
And our customer value
message is: "The ability

87
00:05:21,369 --> 00:05:24,380
to learn independently begins
with Learning Design."

88
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:29,010
These are proposed expressions,
not finalized brand slogans.

89
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:32,898
Whatever we ultimately choose,
our messages must reinforce

90
00:05:32,957 --> 00:05:36,040
a clear and consistent
position in customers' minds.

91
00:05:37,490 --> 00:05:41,600
Finally, let me outline five
strategic priorities for execution.

92
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:45,563
First, we will focus on our
strongest core subjects

93
00:05:45,627 --> 00:05:48,570
rather than promoting
all 17 subjects equally.

94
00:05:49,020 --> 00:05:53,680
This will allow us to build a clear and
differentiated Learning Design approach.

95
00:05:54,380 --> 00:05:57,112
Second, we will strengthen
the connection between

96
00:05:57,168 --> 00:05:59,510
assessment, Learning Design, and coaching.

97
00:05:59,960 --> 00:06:03,974
Each child's learning needs will be
assessed, the next learning steps will

98
00:06:04,029 --> 00:06:08,260
be designed, and instructors will provide
personalized guidance along the way.

99
00:06:08,960 --> 00:06:12,750
Third, we will continue to emphasize
the role of our instructors.

100
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:17,479
While AI-powered learning solutions
are important, personal guidance

101
00:06:17,542 --> 00:06:22,010
and ongoing learning support remain
key reasons why parents choose JEI.

102
00:06:22,710 --> 00:06:26,365
Fourth, we will communicate a
consistent brand message across

103
00:06:26,425 --> 00:06:30,200
our products, learning centers,
local offices, and advertising.

104
00:06:30,650 --> 00:06:33,136
"Design" and "Self-Learning
Ability" should

105
00:06:33,194 --> 00:06:35,680
remain central to how
we present our brand.

106
00:06:36,380 --> 00:06:40,423
Fifth, we will focus on increasing
value per customer and recognize

107
00:06:40,484 --> 00:06:44,587
the importance of multi-subject
learning, while avoiding competition

108
00:06:44,647 --> 00:06:48,570
based solely on the number of
subjects or overall business scale.

109
00:06:49,270 --> 00:06:53,266
Together, these priorities will
help JEI strengthen its position in

110
00:06:53,326 --> 00:06:57,680
Learning Design and deliver greater
value to children and their families.

111
00:06:59,130 --> 00:07:02,797
To summarize, JEI aims to move
beyond workbooks and establish

112
00:07:02,857 --> 00:07:06,584
a leadership position in Learning
Design by designing learning

113
00:07:06,644 --> 00:07:09,830
to develop children's ability
to learn independently.

114
00:07:10,530 --> 00:07:12,850
To achieve this, we must change first.

115
00:07:13,300 --> 00:07:16,341
When we develop products,
meet customers, and discuss

116
00:07:16,399 --> 00:07:19,440
ideas in meetings, we must
all use the same language.

117
00:07:19,890 --> 00:07:24,180
Starting today, our shared message
is “Designing the Ability to Learn.”

118
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:25,550
Thank you.

119
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,370
Please feel free to ask any questions.

